    "product_id": "ab7af3e5-5912-452b-8ed3-04f95b944557",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 030706\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1205 AM PDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n\n* Above-normal temperatures and dry conditions continue into next \n  week as high pressure dominates.\n\n* Heat risk remains minor with pockets of moderate in Death Valley \n  and in the Colorado River Valley.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Friday.\n\nAbove normal temperatures are expected through this weekend as upper \nlevel ridging remains solidly in place over the western US. As the \nridge builds, afternoon high temperatures will climb to 5-8 degrees \nabove normal for this time of the year. Temperatures may moderate \nslightly late Sunday and Monday as a shortwave tries to move in and \nknocks down the area of high pressure, but temperatures are still \nexpected to remain above normal. The ridge builds back the rest of \nnext week and temperatures will again climb 5-8 degrees above \nnormal. With cooler overnights, HeatRisk should remain Minor (level \n1 of 4) in most locations. The exceptions will be in Death Valley \nwhere moderate to isolated major HeatRisk may develop at times, but \nthis is not abnormal for the low lying desert area. Winds will \nincrease slightly as the shortwave approaches Sunday and Monday, but \nthe probability for impactful wind gusts over 40 mph is less than \n10% across the region. With building high pressure, it will remain \ndry with no precipitation chances through the period. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds \ncontinue to be light and follow typical, daily patterns. Chance of \nseeing 10+ knot sustained winds is 10% or less throughout the TAF \nperiod. Few to scattered high clouds.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Easterly to southerly \ngusts of 15-20 knots possible (50%) across western portions of the \nforecast area Saturday afternoon. Elsewhere, winds remain light and \ndiurnal with speeds less than 10 knots. VFR conditions prevail with \njust high clouds passing through.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Nickerson\nAVIATION...Woods\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
